BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:starship-15@superchargeddaily.com
DTSTAMP:20261030T204448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:[Date only] Starship Flight 15
DESCRIPTION:NET date · time unconfirmed\nNET 12 November on the FAA's 29 O
 ct 2026 air-traffic planning slides (moved from 8 Nov)\, not a SpaceX T-0.
  On the 20 Oct earnings call Musk said SpaceX expects Flight 15 next month
  and will try to catch both the booster and the ship. Booster 22 completed
  a full-duration 33-engine static fire on 25 Oct\, per SpaceX. NASASpacefl
 ight and Next Spaceflight report a Ship 42 single-engine static fire at Ma
 ssey’s on 26 Oct\, then a six-engine\, roughly 60-second full-duration f
 ire on 27 Oct 2026\, about 4:46pm CDT (about 21:46 Irish time). SpaceX has
 n’t posted about the Ship 42 fires. Both Flight 15 vehicles have now sta
 tic-fired. Still no FAA licence and no SpaceX date.\nhttps://compass.atfm.
 aero/public_svcdynamic/getfile?download=false&fileuuid=0fb6079b-6d10-4039-
 8766-b3ccb3c877f0\nhttps://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/
 20/spacex-spcx-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\nhttps://x.com/SpaceX/sta
 tus/2114444137067844004\nhttps://www.nextspaceflight.com/starship/hardware
 /80/\nhttps://thespaceroad.com/articles/when-is-starship-flight-15/
LOCATION:Starbase · Pad 2
URL:https://superchargeddaily.com/calendar.html?event=starship-15
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
